  "explanation_short": "The incremental feature analysis shows that adding features sequentially improves model performance, particularly for KNN and RF. The best overall performance is achieved with 11 features, where KNN achieves an R² of 0.8178 and an MSE of 0.01276.",
  "explanation_full": "The incremental feature analysis tracks how model performance (R² and MSE) changes as features are added sequentially. The results demonstrate a general trend of increasing performance (higher R² and lower MSE) as more relevant features are included. For instance, with 11 features (VFA -> Butyrate -> Acetate -> VSS -> Propionate -> Ethanol -> COD-O -> pH -> ORP_Low -> ORP_Mid -> Sucrose_Degradation), the KNN model achieves the highest R² (0.8178) and the lowest MSE (0.01276). Similarly, RF also shows strong performance (R²=0.7855, MSE=0.0150). The analysis confirms that the inclusion of all 11 features provides the optimal feature set for maximizing model performance across the tested models.",
